  "answer_text": "Because the NBA is currently in the middle of the **2026 NBA Finals**, the next game on the schedule is **Game 3: San Antonio Spurs at New York Knicks**. \n\n### **Next Game Details**\n* **Matchup:** San Antonio Spurs vs. New York Knicks (The Knicks currently lead the series 2-0)\n* **Date & Time:** Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET\n* **Location:** Madison Square Garden, New York, NY\n\n---\n\n### **Where to Buy Tickets**\nSince this is a high-demand NBA Finals game, tickets on the primary market will be extremely limited or sold out, but you can find plenty of seats available on official resale platforms. Here is where you can secure tickets:\n\n#### **1. The Official NBA Sources**\n* **[NBATickets.com](https://www.nbatickets.com):** This is the NBA's official ticketing portal. It will redirect you directly to the safe, authorized ticket options for the Knicks' home games. \n* **[Ticketmaster](https://www.ticketmaster.com):** Ticketmaster is the **Official Ticket Marketplace of the NBA**. This is the safest place to buy because any tickets sold here are 100% verified and instantly reissued in your name, meaning there is zero risk of getting a counterfeit ticket.\n\n#### **2. Major Secondary Ticket Marketplaces**\nIf you want to compare prices and seat locations, these trusted resale sites are excellent options and offer buyer-protection guarantees:\n* **[StubHub](https://www.stubhub.com):** One of the largest ticket search engines with a \"FanProtect\" guarantee. \n* **[SeatGeek](https://www.seatgeek.com):** The official ticketing partner of several NBA teams. They feature a \"Deal Score\" system that rates whether you are getting a good price for the seat's location.\n* **[Vivid Seats](https://www.vividseats.com):** Another highly popular secondary market that frequently runs rewards programs for frequent buyers.\n\n### **Tips for Buying NBA Finals Tickets:**\n* **Beware of Scams:** Avoid buying tickets from social media, Craigslist, or street sellers. Always use verified platforms that offer buyer guarantees.\n* **Mobile Entry Only:** The NBA uses strictly digital/mobile ticketing. You will need a smartphone with the Ticketmaster app or the team's official app to scan your ticket at the Madison Square Garden gates. \n* **Watch for Price Drops:** For marquee events like the Finals, ticket prices sometimes drop slightly in the hours leading up to tip-off as sellers try to unload remaining inventory. However, waiting too long runs the risk of missing out on the best seats.",
